    /// <summary>
    /// MLEDIT's tees (CT, OT, MT) and the picks of a corner joint against the records AutoCAD 2021 left (accoreconsole, read
    /// back through <c>DxfOut</c> of a <c>Wblock</c>), STANDARD at scale 20 justified at the top. A tee works on the pair of
    /// segments whose lines meet nearest the two picks along the multilines, and not on the ones the picks lie on: the first
    /// multiline (the stem) is run on past its free end, the second must be met on one of its segments (the end of its last is
    /// not on it); the pair that can be made nearest the picks is taken, which end of the stem is kept is the side of the
    /// meeting the stem's pick is on, and where no pair can be made the nearest pair of all says whether it is <c>Invalid
    /// operation on a self intersecting multiline.</c> (the stem run on past its free end to a second met past a vertex of
    /// its own on an end segment, or the stem met past a vertex of its own and the second past its free end, the stem's start
    /// caps put off and nothing else changed) or <c>These multilines do not intersect.</c>. The same multiline picked twice
    /// is nothing said by a cross or a tee (AutoCAD asks for the first again) and the usual message for a corner joint, and
    /// a corner joint picked on the very point the lines meet keeps the start of that multiline. A break across the second
    /// that reaches the end of its last segment leaves nothing beyond it, as a cross's does. Each row is the option, the
    /// points of the first multiline, those of the second, where each is picked, and what AutoCAD answered: its message, then
    /// the two multilines each as its flags and its vertices with the stretches of each element after the offset in braces,
    /// as <see cref="MlineJoinNearCornerTests"/> writes them. Rows where two multilines run into each other are left out;
    /// meetings near a corner of a three-segment second are in <see cref="MlineTeeThreeSegmentTests"/>.
    /// </summary>
    public class MlineTeePairTests
